{#
  Work claimed, and work proved.

  The two counts sit side by side and are never added. A task marked done is
  somebody's statement that they changed something; a verified fix is a later
  scan observing the check pass. Summing them would let the claim inflate the
  proof, which is the one arithmetic this product refuses everywhere else.
#}
<h2 class="section-title" id="remediation">Remediation progress</h2>

<table class="kpis">
  <tr>
    <td><div class="kpi">
      <span class="kpi-tag">In flight</span>
      <span class="kpi-value">{{ report.remediation.open_tasks }}</span>
      <span class="kpi-label">Open remediation tasks</span>
    </div></td>
    <td><div class="kpi">
      <span class="kpi-tag">Claimed</span>
      <span class="kpi-value">{{ report.remediation.completed_in_window }}</span>
      <span class="kpi-label">Tasks marked done in the last {{ report.window_days }} days</span>
    </div></td>
    <td><div class="kpi">
      <span class="kpi-tag">Observed</span>
      <span class="kpi-value">{{ report.posture.verified_resolved_in_window }}</span>
      <span class="kpi-label">Findings verified fixed in the last {{ report.window_days }} days</span>
    </div></td>
    <td><div class="kpi">
      <span class="kpi-tag">Overall</span>
      <span class="kpi-value">{{ (report.remediation.remediation_rate * 100) | round(0) | int }}%</span>
      <span class="kpi-label">Share of findings ever raised that are now verified fixed</span>
    </div></td>
  </tr>
</table>
{% if report.remediation.cancelled_tasks %}
<p class="small muted">
  {{ report.remediation.cancelled_tasks }} task{{ '' if report.remediation.cancelled_tasks == 1 else 's' }} cancelled.
</p>
{% endif %}
<p class="footnote">
  Work marked done is a claim; a verified fix is an observation. Where the
  first number exceeds the second, the difference is work whose effect
  CloudGuard has not yet seen in the environment — either because no scan has
  run since, or because the change did not have the effect expected.
</p>
